v1.3
    New: last-resort link watchdog (/data/e3372_linkwatch.sh), started
        detached by the service so that it survives the service being
        killed. Every rung of the ladder needs the modem's tty or
        /dev/cdc-wdm0; both vanish when the modem leaves the USB bus, and
        serial-starter then kills the service - so nothing was left to
        reset the USB port, the one action that brings such a modem back.
        The watchdog does only that, once wwan0 has had no address and no
        default route for LINKWATCH_DOWN_SECONDS (15 min by default), at
        most once every 30 min, and never while the session is alive.
        LINKWATCH=0 disables it; LINKWATCH_HCI_RESET=1 additionally allows
        rebinding the USB controller when the modem is not on the bus at
        all (opt-in: it re-enumerates the other devices of that
        controller).
    New: recovery ladder for every state in which the modem cannot be
        dialled. The watchdog used to give up silently whenever the modem
        was not registered (CREG 0/2/3/4): a "Registration denied" from the
        network left the GX offline for 11 days, until a reboot. It now
        escalates, after a grace period, through a network re-selection
        (AT+COPS=2/0), a radio cycle (AT+CFUN=0/1), a modem reset
        (AT+CFUN=1,1) and a USB port reset, with a growing pause between
        full ladders (15 min doubling up to 4 h) and never more than two
        destructive resets per 30 min. The same ladder covers a mute AT
        port, a missing or failed SIM, a data session that will not dial,
        and a session that passes no traffic. The GX itself is never
        rebooted: every action is confined to the modem.
    New: RECOVERY_LEVEL (0-4, 0 = observe only) and RECOVERY_TIMESCALE in
        /data/e3372-config.conf. Heavy commands go through /dev/cdc-wdm0 so
        that a slow answer never blocks the service.
    New: SIM PIN sent from /Settings/Modem/PIN, once; a wrong PIN clears the
        setting (three wrong attempts would lock the SIM). /SimStatus now
        uses the codes the GUI displays (no SIM, PIN, PUK, failure, ...).
    New: recovery state persisted in /run (survives a service restart, not a
        reboot), persistent journal in /data/log/e3372/recovery.log,
        /Recovery/* and /Signal/* paths on D-Bus, signal quality
        (RSSI/RSRP/SINR/RSRQ) logged every minute and on every transition.
    Fix: the dial no longer blocks the service for up to 22 s. The previous
        session is confirmed down before the new one is requested, and the
        re-dial backoff is only reset after 60 s of stable session: 40% of
        the drops used to be a fresh session dying seconds after the dial,
        re-dialled every 30 s.
    Fix: a service restart keeps a session that is already up instead of
        re-dialling it (and cutting the remote access with it).
    Fix: a stale DHCP client no longer blocks the address forever.
    Fix: the connectivity probe accepts several hosts and is suspended for
        6 h instead of being disabled for good.
    Fix: unsolicited modem reports (^RSSI, ^HCSQ, ^MODE, ...) can no longer
        be mistaken for a response; AT^CURC=0 at start.
    Fix: status polling stops at the first timeout, so a mute modem costs
        one timeout per poll instead of six.

v1.2
    Fix: /PPPStatus now follows the Victron PPP_STATUS enum (0 down,
        1 connecting, 2 up). The session-up state was published as 1,
        which the GUI renders as "Data link (PPP) status: connecting"
        even with the connection established. 1 is now published only
        while actually dialling.
    Fix: modem identification (/Model, /IMEI) is retried from the periodic
        update until it succeeds. A single AT timeout at startup used to
        leave both empty until the service was restarted.
    Cleanup: USB_PID removed from e3372-config.conf - nothing ever read it
        (the USB PIDs are hardcoded in the udev rules).
    ReadMe: repository URL corrected (flmusic -> florent1080).

v1.1
    Fix: the data session is now watched and re-dialled automatically.
        The session could drop (operator side) while wwan0 kept its stale
        address and default route. Nothing detected it and nothing re-dialled,
        so the GX lost internet until the next reboot.
    Fix: /Connected no longer forced to 1 by a leftover address on wwan0.
        AT^NDISSTATQRY is now the only source of truth for the data session.
        The UI used to report "Internet: Online" with the session closed.
    Fix: /PPPStatus is now actually published. It was declared once at
        startup and never written, so the UI showed "Data link (PPP) status:
        Offline" permanently, including when the connection worked.
    Fix: e3372_connect.sh no longer opens a serial port. It hardcoded
        /dev/ttyUSB0, which on a Venus OS install is normally a VE.Direct
        adapter and not the modem: the AT commands never reached the modem,
        and the port was switched to 115200 baud under the VE.Direct service.
        Dialling now belongs solely to dbus-modem-e3372.py, which
        serial-starter binds to the modem's real tty.
    Fix: udhcpc no longer runs with -q, so the DHCP client stays resident,
        renews the lease and restores the address and default route.
    Fix: e3372_connect.sh takes a lock; it used to race up to three
        concurrent udhcpc against each other on a single hotplug.
    Fix: the stale address is flushed before re-dialling, so the old default
        route can no longer black-hole traffic.
    Fix: /Settings/Modem/Connect is honoured (connect / hang up on change).
    Fix: the serial port is reopened after an I/O error instead of leaving
        the service permanently deaf.
    New: PROBE_HOST in /data/e3372-config.conf - host pinged periodically to
        detect a session that is up but no longer passing traffic. Set it
        empty to disable when the APN filters ICMP.

v1.0
    initial release
    Huawei E3372h (NCM mode, USB PID 12d1:1506) support for Venus OS
    D-Bus modem service (com.victronenergy.modem) with signal, network, IMEI
    NCM data connection via AT^NDISDUP + DHCP on wwan0
    udev rules for serial-starter and hotplug
    configurable APN via /data/e3372-config.conf
